{"id": "6f9d345c-1382-4291-82d0-ae9e5b73a73b", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Let me check the current configuration of these three resources in eu-central-1 — replication, backups, and failover setup — so I can map them against your RPO 15 min / RTO 1 hour target.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_wGUJ0pxbqPMHh7ZrKnWUWE", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess current disaster-recovery posture of three resources in eu-central-1 (RDS MySQL 'dr-demo-mysql', ElastiCache Valkey 'dr-demo-valkey', and compute/app resource 'dr-demo-players') against a target of RPO 15 minutes and RTO 1 hour for a full Region failure.",
  "context": "Customer wants to know which DR strategy (backup/restore, pilot light, warm standby, multi-site active/active) fits their app backend. Customer/purchase data (MySQL) needs RPO 15min/RTO 1hr on Region failure. The Valkey cache is explicitly rebuildable from the database so it does not need its own replication/failover - it just needs to be re-provisioned and warmed on failover. Need to know what exists today (cross-region read replicas, automated backups, snapshot schedule, Multi-AZ, ElastiCache replication group config, what 'dr-demo-players' actually is - ECS/EKS/EC2/Lambda - and whether it's deployed in a second region or has IaC/AMI/container image ready to redeploy), and whether any AWS Resilience Hub app/assessment, AWS Backup plan, or Route53/Global Accelerator failover routing already exists for these resources.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql", "dr-demo-valkey", "dr-demo-players", "eu-central-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state, not historical",
  "criteria": "For MySQL: engine, Multi-AZ setting, automated backup retention window, backup/snapshot frequency, presence of cross-region read replica or AWS Backup cross-region copy, point-in-time-recovery capability. For Valkey: node/replication group topology, snapshot settings, whether it's single-region only (expected). For dr-demo-players: resource type (ECS/EKS/EC2/Lambda/etc), whether multi-region, how it's deployed (IaC, container image, AMI) and how fast it could be redeployed in another region. Also check for any existing Resilience Hub application definition/assessment covering these resources, any AWS Backup plans, and any Route 53 health-check/failover or Global Accelerator config pointing at a secondary region."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check DR posture of dr-demo-mysql, dr-demo-valkey, dr-demo-players in eu-central-1"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "39807989-5fa1-4f83-a1b2-01b86323c1ab", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Turns out dr-demo-players is actually a DynamoDB table, not a compute resource like ECS/EKS/EC2/Lambda, which resolves the earlier ambiguity. The real compute pieces are the ECS service dr-demo-api, the Lambda consumer dr-demo-consumer, and an SQS queue dr-demo-events.

I should pull the DynamoDB table's details — billing mode, PITR status, and global table/multi-region settings. There's also an Aurora cluster "database-1," but it's untagged and unrelated to this DR demo, so I'll disregard it and focus on gathering the DynamoDB configuration.

"}], "parent_id": "bbcc193b-d7d8-401c-8ff8-63733bdf6f20"}

{"id": "fc3a8e73-01b4-4500-b2b2-e40ce181a341", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Since describe_table got blocked as mutative, which seems odd for a read-only call, I should try alternative read paths like list_global_tables, describe_global_table, or list_backups to get the table information I need another way.

The CloudFormation template already confirms this is a plain DynamoDB table resource, and we know PITR is enabled with a 7-day recovery window, giving near-zero RPO in-region. What I still need to determine is whether it's set up as a Global Table for multi-region resilience, so I should check list_global_tables alongside list_backups.

"}], "parent_id": "bbcc193b-d7d8-401c-8ff8-63733bdf6f20"}

{"id": "fb5b8b72-45b9-49c5-8019-176b3f113c1d", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The AWS Backup plan "dr-demo-daily" does have a cross-region copy rule to eu-west-1, running daily at 03:00 UTC - so cross-region copy is configured, but only once a day, giving an RPO of up to 24 hours rather than the 15-minute target.

I need to check which resources are actually covered by the "dr-demo-tagged" selection - likely RDS and DynamoDB based on project tags - by pulling the backup selection details, and then verify in the eu-west-1 vault that recovery points are actually landing there.

"}], "parent_id": "bbcc193b-d7d8-401c-8ff8-63733bdf6f20"}
